**I support continuing under D439, with a $0 audit of the postponement path next.** I do not support writing or sending the proposed ladder change yet: the 38 answers are a census of a wording shape, not 38 demonstrated errors or 38 independent questions.

My reversible decisions:

1. **Starting library:** use a library built from real earlier material for the next product-oriented test. Preserve empty-start tests as separately labelled diagnostics and keep the frozen ruler’s own conditions unchanged. D559’s wider confirmation was not Alex’s recorded answer; this is a council choice under D439. Reverse it on Alex’s word or evidence that a different starting condition better tests the intended use. [D559](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:6976).

2. **Six lines:** keep Alex’s accepted lines and the existing accounting in force. Report reader disagreements and diagnostic recounts beside the result; they do not constitute a pass or silently remove XR. Revisit their role if Alex decides otherwise or a reviewed control demonstrates that the accounting cannot reliably apply the lines. [D400](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4376).

3. **Postponement:** provisionally use **Still open** for a formal postponement where the event itself remains possible and has not been abandoned or rejected. Record the cost plainly: a question asking whether it happens by a date can close showing “Still open” even after that date has passed. Reverse this reading if Alex rules otherwise or review of worked cases shows it misstates the question an analyst is holding. This is a council interpretation, not a rule Alex already settled. [D409](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4502), [boundary cases](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/BOUNDARY-CASES.md).

4. **D520 and the two invented directions:** provisionally retain the running behavior while work is untested. For a future reviewed version, the product target should be to distinguish an answer with no stated sizing from a supported estimate, and to avoid assigning a favorable direction where none is registered. Neither target proves a label, no-band rule or composite is workable. Reverse the provisional choices on Alex’s word or a test showing a better presentation; do not alter the running product on this decision. [D520](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unsupported/DESIGN-NOTE.md), [decision page](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md:145).

5. **P1:** leave the existing snapshot rule in force for now. P1 can be reviewed as a council decision if live operation becomes the next concrete step; this decision does not authorize a restart, deployment or publication. [Decision page](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/DECISION-PAGE-2026-11-16.md:185).

**The next step is a $0 audit and sizing of the postponed-event class**, not yet a prompt sentence. Read the 38 answers by distinct topic and matter, their complete generated rungs and original requests, beside the source articles and the provisional rule. Include guards for cancellation, a delay still inside the deadline, a changed decision, and an authority’s proceeding; map both the model-written decision and the generic text code appends.

That last part matters: the model’s first sentence is not the whole Ruled-out condition. Code also admits another decision against the event, so a prompt-only exclusion must be checked against the full rung before it can be called a fix. [Rung writer](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step4-2026-11-10/ladder/ladder_step.py:300).

A result that advances the path is a general, sourced mechanism affecting multiple distinct matters, with a proposed change that makes the worked cases unambiguous and has a prewritten control and harm test. Close this proposed route if the audit finds only isolated misapplications, no general rule that preserves the guards, or a change that merely moves the ambiguity. The 37 company-delay answers include **29 passed by both first readers** under the existing form; changing the product meaning would change their assessment, not reveal 37 previously established failures. [Census](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/unlisted-parts/fresh-a2/postponement/RESULT.md).

I cannot establish from the record that this is the *largest* gate-moving repair. It is a product-visible class with an existing census and a concrete next test; the audit will decide whether it is a defensible candidate. Any later send needs its own reviewed design and ceiling.

CONSENSUS: no, because the proposed sentence and paid probe are premature; adopt the reversible positions above and first audit the full postponement path at $0.
